            <ArticleTitle>Real-world Evidence and the 'Unsticking' of Health Care Data.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>29</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ideally, real-world evidence would be continually looped back into the drug development process. There is a deep reservoir of information about side effects, adherence, and differences in efficacy among subpopulations embedded in the various sources of real-world evidence. Extracting it will take hard work.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
